  "query_preview": "..FOR EXTREME SOUTHWESTERN CALIFORNIA INCLUDING ORANGE...\nSAN DIEGO...WESTERN RIVERSIDE AND SOUTHWESTERN SAN BERNARDINO\nCOUNTIES...\n\n\n...UPDATED AVIATION, MARINE, AND BEACHES DISCUSSIONS...\n\nA weak troughing pattern will continue across the region today into \nThursday. This will bring temperatures near to slightly below normal \nwith quiet weather. The marine layer will begin to build further in \nthe days ahead with better chances for low clouds to fill parts \nof the coastal basin each night and morning. \n\nA low pressure system currently over British Columbia will move \nsouthward Thursday into Friday, near the coasts of Washington and \nOregon. As it does so, the troughing pattern will become stronger, \nbringing in slightly cooler weather and a deeper marine layer. The \nmarine layer may become saturated enough by early Friday morning \nthrough Saturday morning produce isolated light showers for \ncoastal areas and western valleys as high-res models are beginning\nto suggest, so chances for rain are around 15-25% in the forecast.\n\nA large area of moisture in the form of a subtropical low pressure \nsystem that we have been watching the past few days, continues to \nlook likely to form off to our southwest Friday into Saturday. \nThere continues to be model differences on exactly where this \nsystem tracks into the Halloween weekend. Some show the system \nmoving further north across SoCal, which would give us a more wet \nscenario. Others keep the system further south toward San Diego \nand into Baja California, which would not be as wet. Both these \ntales favor San Diego County receiving the most rain overall. \n\nIn terms of timing and how much rainfall we see is still in \nquestion. The heaviest rain may begin as early as Saturday afternoon \nstarting from west to east, though would not be surprised if this is \ndelayed toward an evening start. Chances for the heaviest rain \ngreatly increase later Saturday night into Sunday morning area \nwide, with rain showers diminishing Sunday night. NBM shows \nchances for weekend rain totals over 1 inch to be near 55-70% \nacross western San Diego County, as well as all mountain areas \nacross SoCal. The chances lower near 35-45% for much of Orange \nCounty, the Inland Empire and the desert regions. These chances \nand the forecast will likely change some in the coming days, so \nplease be prepared for wetter than normal Halloween weekend and \nkeep an eye on the forecast.\n\nStarting Monday into the middle next week, high pressure moves in \nfrom the west. This will bring temperatures closer to average near \nthe coast, and about 5 degrees below normal for inland areas. \nAnother low pressure system far off the coast may influence the \nweather later next week.",
